  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday morning through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 251 PM EST Wed Nov 25 2026\n\nNo significant changes to the long term period with this forecast \nupdate. A cool and cloudy start to kick off the long term period as \na strong low pressure system in place just to our north lifts \nnortheast towards the New England States. Some flurries are not out \nof the question early Friday mainly at the higher elevations but \nthat potential will gradually wane as the main weather system lifts \nnortheast. At this time no significant impacts are anticipated \nhowever temperatures in North GA will bear watching through the day \nfor any 'refreezing potential' Friday Night. Otherwise, seasonably \ncool and mostly dry through Saturday. Guidance suggests another \nweather system, either a closed low or open wave, will sweep through \nthe area late this weekend bringing another chance of rainfall to \nthe area. Additionally, south winds ahead of this system will bring \nslightly warmer temperatures to the area through early next week. \nForecast highs will rise to the into the 50s at the higher \nelevations and 60s elsewhere.",
